proposed_comments.body:
### Isolate independent Store ID lookup failures

**Severity:** `high`

A COM or invalid-operation failure from one `FindPackages` task faults `Task.WhenAll`, causing the outer handler to discard successful results for every other Store ID. Catch the expected per-ID failures inside the task and return a null package for only that ID; cancellation should still propagate.

```suggestion
                    try
                    {
                        var findResult = await Task.Run(() => catalog.FindPackages(options), cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
                        if (findResult.Status != FindPackagesResultStatus.Ok)
                        {
                            CoreLogger.LogWarning($"Microsoft Store package lookup failed for '{id}': {findResult.Status}");
                            return (id, (CatalogPackage?)null);
                        }

                        if (findResult.Matches.Count > 0)
                        {
                            return (id, findResult.Matches[0].CatalogPackage);
                        }

                        return (id, (CatalogPackage?)null);
                    }
                    catch (OperationCanceledException)
                    {
                        throw;
                    }
                    catch (Exception ex) when (ex is COMException or InvalidOperationException)
                    {
                        CoreLogger.LogWarning($"Microsoft Store package lookup failed for '{id}': {ex.Message}");
                        return (id, (CatalogPackage?)null);
                    }
```

### Isolate Store package status inspection

**Severity:** `high`

`InstalledVersion` is not refreshed before it is read, and an inspection failure for one package is handled only by the outer pass-level catch. Refresh and isolate each package inspection so one failing Store package does not prevent later extensions from being evaluated; cancellation should still propagate.

```suggestion
                                try
                                {
                                    await catalogPackage.CheckInstalledStatusAsync();
                                    entry.IsInstalled = catalogPackage.InstalledVersion is not null;
                                    entry.IsInstalledStateKnown = true;
                                }
                                catch (OperationCanceledException)
                                {
                                    throw;
                                }
                                catch (Exception ex)
                                {
                                    LogCheckWinGetPackageStatusError(_logger, ex);
                                }
```
